* -dialect=c32 leaves out junk after a set's or equ's value, but \@ (Len\@ set *-Beg\@ in a
* macro) is part of the name: was cut to *-Beg, undefined. The bytes are C 3.2's R68's in vDos
* (the quotes stripped from an argument: dc.b abc, an external).
* fixed: 0d7477f 2026-10-12 r68togas: -dialect=c32's junk after a value not at a \@ or parameter
* options: -dialect=c32
* expect text: 01000100 4e71
STR macro
 dc.b Len\@
Beg\@ equ *
 dc.b \1
Len\@ set *-Beg\@
 endm
 psect c32_set_macro_at,0,0,0,0,0
 STR "abc"
 STR 'cd'
 nop
 ends
